{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017143-goetic-demons-from-more-abstract-vices","id":1017143,"title":"Goetic Demons from more abstract Vices.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-14T10:35:05-08:00","id":1017143,"title":"Goetic Demons from more abstract Vices.","content":"My character is binding a Goetic Familiar, and with a Vice of Controlling, it's a bit difficult to pin down all the possibilities of how it can go. So far I've come up with Arrogance, Dominance, Mania, and Obsession(mundane obsession). Anybody see any other ideas that I've missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:27:37-08:00","id":1017173,"title":"","content":"Goetia don't need to be tied to a Vice; they can come from any part of a person's psyche, including things not explicitly detailed as Vices. They can even be noble parts of you (or at least the parts you think are noble).<br /> <br /> If you want something representing the character's controlling, domineering nature, I would go with simply defining it in those terms and no further. The goetic entity is simply, in summary, the character's need to dominate and control.<br /> <br /> Also, goetia aren't called demons anymore; not in the rules, at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:40:56-08:00","id":1017189,"title":"","content":"Mind you if he's binding his Vice to act as his familiar that means that he no longer has a Vice in his Oneiros, which means that he can't regain WP for fulfilling it, and he'd also lose the impulse to be controlling since it would be externalized. I actually have a player who did this with his ability to feel regret. He's an amazing asshole. Naturally, he doesn't miss the ability to regain WP via fulfilling his Vice either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T11:45:34-08:00","id":1017191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1017143-goetic-demons-from-more-abstract-vices?p=1017189#post1017189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you if he's binding his Vice to act as his familiar that means that he no longer has a Vice in his Oneiros, which means that he can't regain WP for fulfilling it, and he'd also lose the impulse to be controlling since it would be externalized. I actually have a player who did this with his ability to feel regret. He's an amazing asshole. Naturally, he doesn't miss the ability to regain WP via fulfilling his Vice either.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is why he's specifically binding it, really. Also, side question, but are you limited to just 1 Familiar? I remember 1E having a Merits for multiple Spirit Familiars, but nothing has appeared in the 2e Core.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:07:02-08:00","id":1017198,"title":"","content":"There's no rules against it, to my knowledge. In theory, you could have a small army of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2855-axelgear","name":"Axelgear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2855_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1450"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T12:45:18-08:00","id":1017222,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you can have as many familiars as you buy Merit dots for or bind with Adept level spells.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T13:02:57-08:00","id":1017243,"title":"","content":"Oh good, then it won't be an issue with my other Familiar, a Spirit of Evening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}